{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"USN-9180-1","published":"2026-11-20T02:34:22Z","modified":"2026-11-24T15:01:42.988112122Z","related":["UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114938","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114939","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114940","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114941","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114942","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114943","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114944","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114945","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114946","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114947"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-114938","CVE-2026-114939","CVE-2026-114940","CVE-2026-114941","CVE-2026-114942","CVE-2026-114943","CVE-2026-114944","CVE-2026-114945","CVE-2026-114946","CVE-2026-114947","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114938","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114939","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114940","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114941","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114942","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114943","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114944","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114945","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114946","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-114947"],"summary":"openjdk-25-crac vulnerabilities","details":"Albert Yang and Quang Luong discovered that the Compiler component of CRaC\nJDK 25 did not correctly handle certain inputs. A remote attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or execute arbitrary\ncode. (CVE-2026-114938)\n\nIt was discovered that the JGSS component of CRaC JDK 25 did not correctly\nauthenticate users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to read\nor modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114939)\n\nNicholas Carlini discovered that the JSSE component of CRaC JDK 25 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto read or modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114940)\n\nIt was discovered that the Compiler component of CRaC JDK 25 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto cause a denial of service or to read or modify sensitive data.\n(CVE-2026-114941)\n\nIt was discovered that the Libraries component of CRaC JDK 25 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto cause a denial of service or to read or modify sensitive data.\n(CVE-2026-114942)\n\nIt was discovered that the Hotspot component of CRaC JDK 25 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto cause a denial of service or to modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114943)\n\nAlexander Dezhinov, Stanislav Dukhin, Nikita Kozlov, and Binbin Xu\ndiscovered that the Core Java Libraries component of CRaC JDK 25 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114944)\n\nIt was discovered that the Libraries component of CRaC JDK 25 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114945)\n\nIt was discovered that the Compiler component of CRaC JDK 25 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto read or modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114946)\n\nJuraj Somorovsky, Maximilian Radoy, and Sven Hebrok discovered that the\nJSSE component of CRaC JDK 25 did not correctly authorize users. A remote\nattacker could possibly use this issue to modify sensitive data.\n(CVE-2026-114947)\n\nIn addition to security fixes, the updated packages contain bug fixes, new\nfeatures, and possibly incompatible changes.\n\nPlease see the following for more information:\nhttps://openjdk.org/groups/vulnerability/advisories/2026-11-17","affected":[{"package":{"name":"openjdk-25-crac","ecosystem":"Ubuntu:26.10","purl":"pkg:deb/ubuntu/openjdk-25-crac?arch=source&distro=stonking"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"25.0.5.1+2-0ubuntu1~26.10.1"}]}],"versions":["25.0.2+10-0ubuntu1","25.0.3+9-0ubuntu1","25.0.4+7-0ubuntu1","25.0.5.0.3+1-0ubuntu2~26.10.1"],"ecosystem_specific":{"availability":"No subscription required","binaries":[{"binary_name":"openjdk-25-crac-demo","binary_version":"25.0.5.1+2-0ubuntu1~26.10.1"},{"binary_name":"openjdk-25-crac-jdk","binary_version":"25.0.5.1+2-0ubuntu1~26.10.1"},{"binary_name":"openjdk-25-crac-jdk